      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Cloud Vision**\n\nOkay, I've decided to go with Google Cloud Vision AI. It seems like the most straightforward and effective option for this image labeling project, given its concrete capabilities. Now, I need to start writing the Python code to interact with the API. This requires authentication and handling the image data.\n\n\n**Implementing the Code**\n\nI'm now focused on the code itself, starting with the `detect_image_labels.py` file. I'll integrate Google Cloud Vision AI, importing the `google.cloud.vision_v1` client and creating the `ImageAnnotatorClient`. I'll load the image and call `label_detection`, then ensure the output is concise. The code will be self-contained, assuming the necessary library is installed, with no extras.\n\n\n",
